# Per-file merge driver for upstream-commit-review.
#
# This file is symlinked into .git/info/attributes by scripts/lib.sh
# during pre-flight, so it does NOT need to be tracked in the repo or
# applied to upstream's working tree.  Mergiraf is registered as a
# merge driver in scripts/lib.sh via `git config`.
#
# Languages mergiraf supports as of late 2025: C/C++, Java, Rust,
# Python, Go, JSON, YAML, ~33 total.  Emacs Lisp and Texinfo are NOT
# yet supported, so .el / .texi files keep Git's default text merge.

*.c        merge=mergiraf
*.h        merge=mergiraf
*.cc       merge=mergiraf
*.cpp      merge=mergiraf
*.hh       merge=mergiraf
*.hpp      merge=mergiraf
